      "content": "but isn't it a bit a stretch to call it just \"survival\" when he literally turned on his own city and helped the Spartans? like, at what point does being a \"realist\" just become being a traitor? it seems like you're brushing off the idea that his actions were fundamentally destructive to the democracy he was supposed to serve.",
